WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.040
 Thank you, you can create a verdict for one presentation. Thank everyone for

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:14.000
 coming here.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:19.120
 Thank you to the entire Councilor Corps who's right here. Also I want to say a

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:23.000
 special welcome to our Council General Gassack from Boulder.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:28.810
 It's quite impressive. One of my father's most amazing accomplishments was when

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:34.130
 he got together with Brad Hall, who was sitting over there, and Dave Kudhi, who

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:35.000
 was sitting over there.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:40.390
 And they developed the initiative to have a nonstop weekly container service

00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:44.360
 directly between Cleveland and Boulder. It's an amazing feat we have now, and

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:50.240
 it comes every two weeks of direct shipment from here to Althorpe. It's

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:51.000
 fantastic.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:56.270
 Trading nations sell the bill to war. That was my father's favorite city. And

00:00:56.270 --> 00:01:02.100
 he lived that city. I remember growing up in many evenings, Arnie would call

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:09.000
 and ask my mom, who sits right over there, to hang up.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:15.580
 It should mind if he brought an international client or two, or five, or eight,

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:21.990
 over in about 30 minutes or so, that my mom was able to whip up an incredible

00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:23.000
 feast.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:27.460
 At moments and moments in time, we always had a wonderful evening while we used

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:31.780
 our hands and feet to try to communicate with the fascinating people from all

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:33.000
 over the world.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:37.890
 It was scary too. We grew up when there was a real iron curtain. A lot of you

00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:43.190
 probably remember that one. When he went there, he was gone for six weeks, and

00:01:43.190 --> 00:01:47.000
 you would not get any information or communication near that time.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:50.560
 And then suddenly he would bring it here again. And he had these wonderful

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:55.240
 stories where he was jogging with the Russian army, or climbing the Great Wall

00:01:55.240 --> 00:02:00.470
 of China, and how he sold truckload plumbing supplies and traded them for a

00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:02.000
 part of the grain.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:07.080
 I mean, trading nations sell them to war, so for all of our cities, let's keep

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:09.000
 trading. Thank you.

